\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Observed and Formula FLOPs. Observed data points fall mostly on the dotted line plotted from formulas.}}{23}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Observed and Formula memops. Observed data points fall mostly on the dotted line plotted from formulas.}}{27}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces FLOPs: Relative error of Formula vs Observed. Very close fit by the formula, and flop count is determined entirely by compression combination.}}{28}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces memops: Relative error of Formula vs Observed. Close fit by most formulas, variability due to the effect of variability of sparsity patterns.}}{29}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Runtime Performance: Timestamp Cycles. Crossover points at 0.7\% density when performing a simple dense x dense is better.}}{30}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Roofline Model. Sparse formats are entirely memory bound.}}{31}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces Diagonal Matrix Results. Poor performance compared to simple global compression, but optimal micro-format selection wins over naive format selection.}}{32}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces Block Size Performance Impact. Performance degrades as block sizes increase.}}{33}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Thread Count Performance Impact. At matrix sizes that can be solved, threading provides minimal benefit beyond 2 threads.}}{34}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.10}{\ignorespaces Kronecker Graph Sweep (AS-Newman). Sparse BLIS performs very poorly compared to a global compression strategy, this worsens as matrix size increases.}}{35}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.11}{\ignorespaces Kronecker Graph Sweep (AS-Newman). Sparse BLIS performs very poorly compared to a global compression strategy, this worsens as matrix size increases.}}{36}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.12}{\ignorespaces Kronecker Graph k=10 (AS-Newman) block size sweep. Block dispatch overhead generally decreases as block size increases, but not nearly enough to be comparable to simple global compression.}}{37}{}%
